                "senderName": "NWS Pueblo CO",
                "headline": "Flood Warning issued October 2 at 3:25PM MDT until October 4 at 8:00AM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO",
                "description": "...The Flood Warning is extended for the following rivers in\nColorado...\n\nPurgatoire River Near Purgatoire R near Las Animas affecting Bent\nCounty.\n\nFor the Purgatoire River...including Purgatoire near Las Animas...\nMinor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Purgatoire River near Purgatoire R near Las Animas.\n\n* WHEN...Until Sunday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 12.0 feet, Moderate Flood. Moderate agricultural\nflooding occurs in low lying areas along the river.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 3:15 PM MDT Friday the stage was 8.5 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage late\nthis afternoon to a crest of 10.8 feet early tomorrow afternoon.\nIt will then fall below flood stage Sunday afternoon.\n- Flood stage is 9.0 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 10.5\nfeet on 08/19/2004.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nMotorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued late tonight at 330 AM MDT.",
